It has become increasingly tedious to use the Logical grids to manage Chunk Surface modifications through Cell Triangulations
The proposal is to introduce a graph abstraction between the Grids and The Mesh/Triangulation.

The graph nodes are the Grid Data points, supplemented by the cell center points, while the edges of the graph are 
the sides of the triangulations.

ChunkGraphNode [Id] => CellSummitPoint [DataGridIndex,()]
                    => CellCenterPoint [CellIndex,[ImpactingDataIndexes],()]
        * GetPosition()
        * TriangulationVertices[6] GetTriVertices()
        * ComputeModificationRequest()<==IGraphDataAware
        * ApplyModification <== ConformalEditor
      
ChunkGraphEdge [eid] => ([Id#1],[Id#2]) Key, unordered
         * TriangulationEdges[2] ~TriangulationEdges
         * ComputeModificationRequest()<==IGraphDataAware
         * ApplyModification <==Conformal Editor       
        
TriangulationVertex : TVId 
         => [TEId  => TriangulationVertex] (neighbors)
         => TId 

TriangulationEdge : TEId
        => TId triangle
        => (TVidSource,TVidTarget) vertices unordered tuple
        => idx (Triangulation's edge index)
        
GraphTriangulation 
    =>Triangulation
    =>[TVId#1,TVId#2,TVId#3] vertices
    =>[TEId#1,TEId#2,TEId#3] edges
                